    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d577">

                <pb facs="0512" n="502" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg502"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00B/8–2449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Jones</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-08-24T15:00:00+08:00">August 24, 1949—3
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 24—9:40 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1885. Bearing upon extent to which CCP draws inspiration from Sun Yat-sen
                    doctrine as against Marxism–Leninism–Stalinism, we <pb facs="0513" n="503"
                        xml:id="pg503"/> note that to best of our knowledge Chinese Communists have
                    held no commemoratory services or celebrations at Sun Yat-sen mausoleum since
                    their take-over of Nanking last April. Neither have we heard of Sun’s picture
                    being used at public meetings as are those of Lenin, Stalin, Mao and Chu.<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d577-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent Department 1885; repeated Shanghai 1036, Canton 793.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jones</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d577-f1" n="3" xml:id="d577-f1-content">
                <p>Chu Teh, Commander in Chief of Chinese Communist armies.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
